.TH EL_SOURCE 3 "2026-05-30" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
el_source \- load editline commands from a configuration file
.SH LIBRARY
Editline library (libedit, \-ledit)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <histedit.h>
.PP
.BI "int el_source(EditLine *el, const char *file);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR el_source ()
reads editline commands from
.I file
and applies them to
.IR el .
.PP
If
.I file
is NULL,
.BR el_source ()
loads the default per-user configuration file,
typically
.BR ~/.editrc .
.PP
Command syntax is described in
.BR editrc (5).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success and \-1 on error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid argument.
.TP
.B ENOENT
Requested configuration file was not found.
.TP
.B EACCES
Permission denied while reading configuration.
.TP
.B EIO
I/O error while reading the configuration file.
.TP
.B EPROTO
A command line could not be parsed.
.SH EXAMPLES
The following program loads the default per-user
.B .editrc
file into a new session:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
#include <histedit.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int
main(void)
{
    EditLine *el = el_init("prog", stdin, stdout, stderr);

    if (el_source(el, NULL) == -1)
        fprintf(stderr, "no .editrc loaded\en");
    el_end(el);
    return 0;
}
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR editline (3),
.BR el_set (3),
.BR history (3),
.BR editrc (5)
